## What I changed

**`src/search.ts`** — one line: the binary search condition was `sorted[mid] <= target` (upper bound: low moves past equals, landing after the last equal element). I changed it to `sorted[mid] < target`, so low only advances past elements strictly below target and the search lands on the first equal element — a proper lower bound. Binary structure, `O(log n)`, unchanged.

**`src/search.test.ts`** — added three tests alongside the existing one:
- target below every element → `0`
- target above every element → the array length
- duplicates → index of the first equal element (including target at the head, in the middle, at the tail, and all-equal arrays with below/above targets)

